Fixtures for the bruce test suite.

docs-fp-o/
  Saved, unmodified, from https://docs.fedoraproject.org, on the dates in
  manifest.json, which also records why each page was chosen. The content is
  by the Fedora Documentation Team and contributors and is licensed CC BY-SA
  4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). These copies are
  shared under the same licence. Each page's source file is named by its
  "Edit this Page" link. scripts/fixtures.py chooses and saves them.

generators/
  Written by hand for this project, under this repository's licence. They
  reproduce only the markup that the invariants register records (I9, I12) of
  Docusaurus, MkDocs Material, Docsy, Furo, the Read the Docs Sphinx theme and
  Antora's tabs, with example.org and github.com/example links in place of the real
  ones. The real pages the markup was read from, on 2026-10-17:
    https://docusaurus.io/docs/installation
    https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/getting-started/
    https://www.docsy.dev/docs/get-started/
    https://pradyunsg.me/furo/quickstart/
    https://docs.readthedocs.io/en/stable/intro/getting-started-with-sphinx.html
  generators/generic/ holds pages with and without landmarks, and with
  competing edit links, for the generic heuristics (D34, D36).

antora/
  content/ is written by hand for this project, under this repository's
  licence: three invented Antora components for `mise run e2e`. ui-bundle.zip
  is Fedora Docs' UI bundle, unmodified, from
  https://gitlab.com/fedora/docs/docs-website/ui-bundle (MPL-2.0), its commit
  and sha256 in ui-bundle.json; scripts/fixtures.py antora-ui vendors it.
  pages/ holds a few pages Antora 3.1.15 built from content/ with that
  bundle, recorded in pages/manifest.json.
